Privacy Policy for Commando Browser
Last updated: [18/09/2026]

This Privacy Policy describes how Commando Browser ("the App", "we", "us") collects, uses, and shares information when you use the App. By using Commando Browser, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.

1. Information We Collect
a) Information You Provide
Commando Browser does not require account creation or login. We do not collect your name, email address, or phone number unless you voluntarily provide it (for example, by contacting us for support).

b) Browsing Activity
As a web browser, the App loads and displays web pages, search results, and content you choose to visit. This browsing activity happens locally on your device. We do not operate our own server that logs the websites you visit.

c) Automatically Collected Information
When you use the App, the following information may be collected automatically:

Device information: device model, operating system version, language, and screen settings.
Approximate location: the App may determine your approximate location based on your IP address (not precise GPS location) to provide region-relevant content such as news, weather, and search results.
Usage data: general app interaction data (e.g., features used, crash reports) used to improve stability and performance.
Advertising identifiers: see Section 2 below.
d) Permissions
The App may request the following device permissions, used only for the stated purpose:

Internet access — required for browsing, search, news, and ad delivery.
Storage — to save downloaded files and cache content (e.g., favicons, images) for faster loading.
Location (if applicable on your device) — to provide local weather and region-relevant content; this can be denied without preventing use of core browsing features.
2. Advertising
Commando Browser displays ads through the Appodeal mediation SDK, which may work with multiple third-party ad networks. These networks may collect and use advertising identifiers (such as the Google Advertising ID) and device information to serve and measure ads, including personalized ads where permitted.

You can opt out of personalized advertising through your device's ad settings (e.g., Android Settings → Privacy → Ads → "Opt out of Ads Personalization"). For details on how Appodeal and its partner networks process data, please refer to Appodeal's own privacy policy at https://www.appodeal.com/privacy-policy/.

3. Third-Party Services
The App integrates with or links to third-party services, including but not limited to:

Google Search / Google News — for search results and news content.
Google Favicon service — to display website icons.
YouTube — for embedded video playback where applicable.
Facebook (facebook.com/reel) — for the Shorts feature, which loads content directly from Facebook within an in-app browser view.
These services are operated by third parties and are governed by their own privacy policies. We do not control how these third parties collect or use your data.

4. Data Sharing
We do not sell your personal information. We may share limited technical data (such as advertising identifiers and device information) with our advertising and analytics partners (e.g., Appodeal and its mediated ad networks) solely to deliver and measure ads and improve app performance.

5. Data Security
We take reasonable measures to protect information processed by the App. However, no method of electronic transmission or storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

6. Children's Privacy
Commando Browser is not directed at children under 13 (or the applicable minimum age in your region). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.

7. Your Choices
You can clear browsing data, cache, and cookies within the App's settings at any time.
You can use the App's Incognito/private browsing mode, which does not retain browsing history after the session ends.
You can manage ad personalization through your device's advertising settings.
8. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date. Continued use of the App after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.

